@startuml requirement-issue-states
' cumin works - states of a requirement issue.
' A state is a label on GitHub. Each arrow is one transition. Its first line names the step of cumin
' that makes it (with the row of issue-states.md), and the second line says what happened.
' One step can have several arrows.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "Draft\n(no status label)" as Draft
state "cumin/status/ready" as Ready
state "cumin/status/planning" as Planning
state "cumin/status/awaiting-owner-review\n(check the sub-issues)" as PlanReview
state "cumin/status/implementing" as Implementing
state "cumin/status/awaiting-owner-review\n(acceptance)" as Acceptance
state "cumin/status/awaiting-owner-decision" as Decision

[*] --> Draft : the Owner writes the requirement,\nadds cumin/type/requirement
Draft --> Ready : the Owner finishes,\nadds cumin/status/ready
Draft --> Implementing : R3 note the start of work:\nthe Owner wrote the sub-issues,\nadded cumin/status/ready to one
Ready --> Planning : R1 request the split:\nthe Planner is asked to split
Planning --> PlanReview : R2 check the split:\nthe split is ready, the Owner checks it
Planning --> Implementing : R2 check the split:\nevery sub-issue is closed
Planning --> Decision : R2 check the split:\nthe split failed the check, or blocked
Decision --> Ready : the Owner fixes the requirement,\nadds cumin/status/ready
PlanReview --> Implementing : R3 note the start of work:\nthe Owner added cumin/status/ready\nto a sub-issue
Implementing --> Implementing : R4 request the acceptance check:\nthe Planner is asked to check
Implementing --> Decision : R4 request the acceptance check:\nthe check returned blocked
Implementing --> Acceptance : R7 hand over the acceptance:\nthe acceptance check is written,\nthe Owner decides
Implementing --> PlanReview : R6 check the remaining sub-issues:\nonly sub-issues without a status label\nremain, the Owner checks them
Acceptance --> Implementing : R3 note the start of work:\nthe Owner sends it back\n(a sub-issue with cumin/status/ready)
Acceptance --> [*] : the Owner closes the requirement issue\n(= accepted)

legend right
  First line of an arrow: the step of cumin (a row of issue-states.md).
  Second line: what happened (the transition).
  An arrow without a row: the Owner acts.
endlegend

@enduml
